id: pm-gjjurs
title: "GH-970: repeated row contracts consume half of agent read output without a suppression contract"
description: "Every read repeats a mostly static row_contract and jq selector in TOON and JSON, consuming 49 to 62 percent of small responses. Add a contract-safe session or invocation mechanism that preserves discoverability while avoiding repeated context spend."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,context-efficiency,output-contracts,row-contract,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-10T22:59:34.849Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T11:02:40.692Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T11:02:00.603Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T11:02:00.603Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Agents can suppress or reference repeated row contracts without suppressing command results; The setting works consistently for TOON JSON CLI SDK and MCP transports through declared runtime contracts; Contract discovery remains available on demand and session behavior is deterministic and measured by the token-surface gate; The row contract is off by default on every read command that currently emits it and is restored by an explicit flag, so the default read pays for data only; Suppression is measured per command against the token-budget-gate corpus, with pm stats named as the reference instance at 285 of 745 default bytes"
parent: pm-5t33or
reporter: GitHub issue #970
severity: medium
environment: pm 2026.8.10 read commands in default TOON and JSON output
repro_steps: "Run comments, notes, show, and list on a small workspace and measure the row_contract block as a share of each response."
resolution: Suppressed repeated row contracts by default at the final composition boundary and added explicit universal restoration.
expected_result: "CLI, SDK, and MCP reads pay for result data by default while contract discovery stays deterministic and opt-in."
actual_result: "Merged outputRowContract contracts, completions, receipt stabilization, calibration, and generated surfaces resolve GH-970."
affected_version: 2026.8.10
component: CLI and SDK output contracts
regression: false
customer_impact: Repeated static metadata consumes backlog-sweep context and reduces useful project information available to agents.
